Cr_rj6zBtx-.content:
Took the opportunity of a superintendent’s conference day to test out a build your own salad concept for our students. A nice mix of locally sourced produce and DOD FFAVORS items.  Space is limited so we had to get creative on how to effectively serve the meal, keep the line moving and have it at make sense. The hot unit was turned into cold wells to start off. We also used the heated food slide for pre portioned protein options so they could be added to salads at the end of the process. Will narrow protein offerings down for students, but today we had grilled chicken, fajita chicken with peppers and onions, popcorn chicken, buffalo chicken, taco meat, Carolina bbq shrimp, and an Indian spiced roasted chickpea. We also offered some crispy chickpeas as a GF crunch for salads instead of croutons. Faculty and staff loved it so we know it will be a big hit with our students too. They say imitation is the best form of flattery so thank you @schoolfoodrocks for being a constant source of inspiration.

Full build your own salad bars coming to menus soon!

